{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsximS3MSjfCUvZ7yGBp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Within-category copying still gives only small effects. The tilt is towards A copying more in layers 11–16: head 16.1 and 16.3 at +0.010 on digits, plus 11.1, 15.3, 16.2 and 12.1. Head 17.3 is the exception, with A copying less. The total over heads is slightly positive (+0.008), but I have no noise baseline yet, so I'm at about 55% that A is sycophantic.\n\nCopying also needs attention to land on the guess, so the change may sit more in what heads attend to (QK) than in OV. Before testing attention direction, I want to see which input tokens' keys and values changed most, relative to their size. I measure it as ‖ΔW_k·diag(1+g)·e_t‖ / ‖W_k·diag(1+g)·e_t‖ per layer.\n\nIf answer-category tokens, or guess-marker words like \"think\", \"guess\", \"believe\" or \"answer\", stand out in the key or value differences, that points to a learned attention-to-guess mechanism. Its sign will then tell me which model attends to the guess more.\n\n```python\nA = Checkpoint(\"A\"); B = Checkpoint(\"B\"); tok = Tokenizer(\"A\")\nE = np.load(\"/work/E.npy\")\nids = np.load(\"/work/ascii_ids.npy\")\n# restrict to \"common\" tokens: space-prefixed words or short tokens, ids < 30000-ish isn't freq-sorted; use all ascii\nX0 = E[ids]\nfor l in [0,2,5,8,11,13,15,16,17]:\n    gi = A.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.input_layernorm.weight\")\n    X = X0*(1+gi)\n    out=[]\n    for p in [\"k_proj\",\"v_proj\",\"q_proj\"]:\n        Wa = A.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.{p}.weight\"); Wb = B.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.{p}.weight\")\n        d = X@(Wa-Wb).T; base = X@Wb.T\n        r = np.linalg.norm(d,axis=1)/np.linalg.norm(base,axis=1)\n        o = np.argsort(-r)[:25]\n        out.append(f\"  {p}: \" + \" \".join(repr(tok.text(ids[i])) for i in o))\n    print(f\"L{l}\"); print(\"\\n\".join(out))\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8369,"cache_read_input_tokens":36982,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8369},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45d9b9f7-5c0c-427a-8806-5390f7a6cfe9","uuid":"a752c65d-91da-46a8-a689-baedb6a2a1a9","timestamp":"2026-11-09T20:11:03.766Z","request_id":"req_011CgsximGrmFRu49XVWtDtG"}
